  "description": "Reid Transit Disc | Commuter bike\nPractical, lightweight and built for everyday journeys – the Reid Bikes Transit Disc is a versatile commuter bike designed for cycling to work, navigating urban streets and exploring local routes.\nBuilt around a lightweight hydroformed alloy frame, the Reid Bikes Transit Disc offers responsive handling and a comfortable ride for regular use. Internal cable routing creates a clean finish while helping protect cables from dirt and the elements. Its rigid steel fork provides a straightforward setup for everyday commuting.\nThe 700c double-wall alloy wheels are fitted with Kenda 700x42mm tyres, offering a balance of rolling efficiency, grip and comfort across roads and cycle paths. The wider tyres help absorb minor bumps and vibrations, making everyday journeys more comfortable.\nA Shimano 2x7-speed drivetrain combines a Prowheel 46/30T chainset with a Shimano 14-34T freewheel, providing a versatile range of gears for tackling hills and maintaining momentum on flatter roads. LTWOO A2 shifters deliver straightforward gear changes, while Tektro MD-M280 mechanical disc brakes with 160mm rotors provide dependable stopping power in different weather conditions.\nDesigned with commuting in mind, the Reid Bikes Transit Disc features frame mounts for fitting a rear luggage rack and mudguards, allowing you to adapt the bike to your daily needs. A chainstay-mounted kickstand adds convenience when parking, while 680mm alloy riser handlebars and a comfortable saddle support a practical riding position.\nThe Reid Bikes Transit Disc is ideal for:\n\nEveryday commuting, with a lightweight alloy frame and responsive handling\n\nUrban cycling, with 700c wheels designed for efficient rolling on paved routes\n\nComfortable everyday rides, with wider 42mm tyres to help absorb road vibrations\n\nTackling varied routes, with Shimano 2x7-speed gearing and a wide-range 14-34T freewheel\n\nConfident braking, with Tektro mechanical disc brakes and 160mm rotors\n\nPractical commuting, with frame mounts for fitting a rear luggage rack and mudguards\n\nConvenient parking, with a chainstay-mounted kickstand",
